        "w": 801,
        "h": 273,
        "opacity": 1,
        "text": "Many early civilizations developed near rivers because water was essential for survival.\nRivers provided drinking water and helped farmers grow crops. Floods left behind rich soil, while boats made travel and trade easier.",
